{
  "_doc": [
    "The boundary sources geo_scripts/build_shapes.py converts into data/geo/shapes/<name>.parquet.",
    "To add one: put its files under data/geo/, add an entry here, run build_shapes.py --only <name>.",
    "name: the source's key; a shape's link is '<name>:<id>'. files: globs relative to data/geo (GeoJSON, Shapefile,",
    "GeoPackage, GeoParquet, KML...; other coordinate systems are converted to lon/lat).",
    "id: the id column(s), first found; or id_from_name: true (the name as a slug, barossa-valley). name / level:",
    "columns, first found (level values zone / region / subregion: one shape per id, the smallest level wins).",
    "id_prefix: 'file' puts the file's region before the id (pfalz_12.parquet -> pfalz:7); file_regions renames a file.",
    "kind: appellation or vineyard (how much detail the display outline keeps). display_merge_m (and display_crs, a",
    "metric projection): parts closer than ~2x that many meters fused in the display outline (INAO's scattered parcels).",
    "assume_crs: the coordinate system",
    "to read the files in when their own tag is wrong (the Weinlagen files say EPSG:4324 for plain lon/lat).",
    "link: how the app's rows find their shape (geo_scripts/link_shapes.py fills the boundary column): table",
    "(appellations or vineyards) and by: an id column of it (strip_prefix: only values starting with it, prefix",
    "removed; region: the row's region before the id, as in the file names, region_aliases renaming some or naming",
    "several files' keys: an id in more than one takes the shape with the row's name, else isn't linked), or 'name'",
    "with country (the appellation's name as a slug, the aliases of geo_scripts/au_gi.py applied), or 'store_name':",
    "the shape's own name in the store within the row's country (country_codes; for ids like PDO-IT-A1234), only when",
    "the when_empty column is empty, aliases ('Country / our name': source_id) first: same denomination, other spelling",
    "or renamed / merged (checked by hand; a sub-zone like Valpolicella Classico isn't one).",
    "'country_name': the shape's id is '<country>:<appellation name>' (admin: build_admin_areas.py).",
    "store_name with 'country': a one-country source whose ids don't carry it (INAO, France). inao_denom: the vines of each",
    "AOC and complementary name (build_inao_areas.py); inao_aires: the areas of appellations and IGPs, for what has no parcels.",
    "inao_denom comes first: a French name with its own INAO outline (Gevrey-Chambertin premier cru) takes it before",
    "the INAO id, which the village and its premier crus share.",
    "link can be a list of rules. A row is linked to the first rule, in this order, that finds its shape.",
    "vineyard: INAO's premiers crus (etl_inao_fr.py vineyards). An installation's own sources go in data/geo/sources.local.json",
    "(same format): one named like a source here replaces it (its own vineyard files: Weinlagen-info's...), others are added."
  ],
  "sources": [
